Early Learning: Sensory Shapes is an audiovisual sensory experience with touch interaction and freehand drawing to encourage creativity and develop hand-eye coordination.

Specifically designed for early learning, studies have shown that young children show more interest in highly contrasting images. Sensory Shapes is ideal for captivating attention and encouraging visual and auditory development.

With full colour, high contrast and colour blind settings, Sensory Shapes is suitable for the learning and development of all children.

Features:
- Black and white, high contrast images for babies;
- Vivid colour images for children;
- Colour blind mode uses specific colours to provide a greater contrast for those with colour blindness #1ineveryclassroom;
- Interactive touch animations;
- Multi-colour, freehand drawing mode encourages creativity and develops hand-eye coordination;
- Compatible with Apple Pencil;
- 14 shapes with vast colour combinations;
- 6 music tracks, courtesy of Bensound.com.
